<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>Squares in a Geometric Pattern</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m01757</md:content-id>
    <md:title>Squares in a Geometric Pattern</md:title>
    <md:uuid>5a2afa81-86e9-444b-87b3-ee39af81dc15</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
    <section class="numbered-exercises" id="sect-00001"><title>Warm Up</title>
      <para id="para-00001">How does each expression represent the number of small squares in the figure?</para>
      <para id="para-00002">
          <media alt="An image of a block of squares. Begin with row 1 at the bottom of the figure. There are eight squares on rows 1, 2, 3 and 4 and five squares on rows 5 - 6. There are six squares missing from the upper right corner of the block.">
            <image mime-type="image/svg+xml" src="../../media/Algebra-1_08_04_02_01.svg"/>
          </media>
        
     </para>
      <!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
      <exercise id="exer-00001">
        <problem id="prob-00001">
          <para id="para-00003">Expression A: <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>6</m:mn><m:mi>·</m:mi><m:mn>8</m:mn><m:mo>–</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mi>·</m:mi><m:mn>3</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00001">
          <para id="para-00004">Compare your answer: </para>
          <para id="para-00005">There are 6 rows with 8 small squares, but from this, 2 rows of 3 small squares have been removed.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Interaction End -->
      <!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
      <exercise id="exer-00002">
        <problem id="prob-00002">
          <para id="para-00006">Expression B: <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mi>·</m:mi><m:mn>8</m:mn><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mi>·</m:mi><m:mn>5</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00002">
          <para id="para-00007">Compare your answer: </para>
          <para id="para-00008">There are 4 rows of 8 small squares, and to this, 2 rows of 5 small squares are added.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Interaction End -->
      <!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
      <exercise id="exer-00003">
        <problem id="prob-00003">
          <para id="para-00009">Expression C: <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>8</m:mn><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>8</m:mn><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>8</m:mn><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>8</m:mn><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>5</m:mn><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>5</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00003">
          <para id="para-00010">Compare your answer: </para>
          <para id="para-00011">This counts each row, starting from the bottom.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Interaction End -->
      <!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
      <exercise id="exer-00004">
        <problem id="prob-00004">
          <para id="para-00012">Expression D: <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>5</m:mn><m:mi>·</m:mi><m:mn>6</m:mn><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mi>·</m:mi><m:mn>4</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00004">
          <para id="para-00013">Compare your answer: </para>
          <para id="para-00014">There are 5 columns of 6 small squares and 3 columns of 4 small squares.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Interaction End -->
      <note id="note-00001">
        <title>Building Character: Proactivity</title>
<media alt="A student with long dark hair raises their hand while sitting at a desk with papers. Behind them is a clock, a bulletin board, a shelf with boxes, and a globe.">
            <image mime-type="image/png" src="../../media/Algebra-1_08_04_02_02.png" height="200"/>
          </media>

            <para id="para-00016">Proactivity is the ability to take initiative. There’s evidence that proactivity is one of the qualities that distinguished the greatest American presidents from their peers.</para>
            <para id="para-00017">Think about your current sense of proactivity. Are the following statements true for you??</para>
            <list id="list-00001">
          <item>I am always looking for better ways of doing things. </item>
          <item>I love to challenge the status quo. </item>
        </list>
            <para id="para-00018">Don’t worry if none of these statements are true for you. Developing this trait takes time. Your first step starts today!</para>
      </note>
    </section>
  </content>
</document>